Given a continuous-lattice projection from D into D', with inclusion i and retraction j, the inclusion of function spaces sends a Scott map f from D to D to the Scott map on D' whose value at x is i(f(j(x))). `functionSpaceInclFun.continuous` says the underlying map x ↦ i(f(j(x))) is continuous for the Scott topologies on D', because it agrees with the composite of the Scott maps i, f, and j. `functionSpaceInclFun.outer_continuous` says the assignment f ↦ i ∘ f ∘ j is continuous for the Scott topologies on the function spaces, because it agrees with conjugation by the pair (i, j).
